## The Framework — Design Outside-In

Design business-first, tech-last. Never start at "which retriever?"

```
OUTCOME  →  AGENT  →  ACTIONS  →  GROUNDING  →  GUARDRAILS  →  PROOF  →  RISKS
(why)      (who/what) (what it    (what it      (what keeps   (does it (what
           does)      DOES)       knows)        it safe)      work?)   breaks?)
```

| Phase | The one question it answers |
|---|---|
| **Outcome** | What business result, measured how? |
| **Agent** | What's the agent's job vs. the human's job? |
| **Actions** | What discrete things must it *do*? |
| **Grounding** | Where does its knowledge come from? |
| **Guardrails** | How do we stay compliant / explainable / safe? |
| **Proof** | How do we know it works before go-live? |
| **Risks** | What could go wrong, and what did we trade off? |

**Maps to presentation sections** ("What We'd Like You to Cover"):
architecture & design decisions · Data Cloud grounding (retriever/chunking/pre-filters) · Equifax integration · APRA compliance & explainability · human-in-the-loop · testing + RAG accuracy · risks.

