**Step 1 — VERIFIED REQUIREMENTS (locked; sources: APRA / ASIC / OAIC official):**

*Requirement vs mechanism:* audit logging, override, telemetry, input sanitisation, explainable logic, escalation = **mechanisms** (step 2), not requirements.

- **APRA CPS 220** (applies to ALL lending): board-approved risk management framework + risk appetite statement; three-lines-of-defence; CRO; independent review ≥ every 3 yrs; board declaration to APRA. → *For the agent:* operate within the RMF; manage the new **model risk** the AI adds; clear human accountability; evidence the controls; escalate breaches.
- **Privacy Act** (applies to ALL): APP 6 (use PII only for collected purpose → no training on customer data); APP 11 (secure PII from unauthorised access/leak); **Part IIIA credit reporting** (Equifax = credit reporting info: consent, permitted-use, retention — CR Code 2014); **APP 8 cross-border** (offshore LLM processing = a disclosure).
- **ASIC RG 209** (CONSUMER credit only — NOT business): 3 RLOs = reasonable inquiries · reasonable steps to **verify** · assess **'not unsuitable'**. ⚠️ Scope nuance: PrimeCapital = SMB/mid-market → much of book is business → RG 209 may not strictly apply. Possible panel clarifying Q.

